WEBVTT

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.860
I-It's Joe!

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:28.980
Hang in there!

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.490
I can't believe you can work out in this heat!

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.940
I just get too hot if I don't break a sweat!

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.450
Hey, ya hear that?

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.450
That whippersnapper sure is something else!

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.170
Carlos Rivera, the world's sixth-ranked...

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.300
Harajima Ryu, the Japanese first-ranked...

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.710
Today's the day they finally cross gloves.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.350
Harajima is confident that he will make it into the world ranking.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.720
Harajima's absolute confidence comes from the fact

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.150
that Carlos was dominated by his partner, Yabuki Joe, in his public sparring match,

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.780
and Harajima has already defeated Yabuki Joe once before.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.370
Yabuki-kun...

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.900
What's the matter? You seem a little down...

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.310
Oh, it's nothing.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.650
I know. You're worried about Joe, aren't you?

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.030
Oh, don't be so ridiculous!

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.280
Honey!

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.900
Hey, what's with that look?

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.120
You shouldn't be teasing your own daughter!

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.040
Besides, what if Nishi hears you?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.410
What'll happen if Nishi-kun hears him?

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.120
Oh, it's nothing, really...

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.250
N-Nothing at all, eh?

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:09.790
I'm back.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.250
Oh, thanks for all the hard work!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.090
Sure had a lot of orders today!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.050
You go ahead and take a break. I'll put on some tea.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:15.920
Sure.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.640
But I can't exactly take my time here.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.930
I gotta head over to Koyama-san's right away...

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.810
You really like your work, don't you, Nishi-kun?

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.100
Since Nishi-kun's going out for work, why don't you go with him?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.640
But I don't want to get in the way of his work.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.320
I'm going for a little walk.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.190
Hey, Noriko!

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.860
N-Noriko, wait!

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.240
Why'd she have to be so headstrong?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.950
Well, I guess that's one of her good qualities.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.000
I think I'll have that tea after all.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.800
Don't you want a wash, Sachi?

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.350
How rude of you! You're talking to a lady!

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.930
A lady, huh?

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.440
Well, a lady needs to be clean!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.350
Oh, please!

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.850
What was that for? Joe, you big dolt!

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.360
What's up? You need something?

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.530
Oh, not really.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.120
I'm just taking a walk to get out of my hot house.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.210
"A walk," she says!

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.870
What a lame excuse!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.090
By the way, how's our Nishi doing?

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.880
Y-Yes, he's working hard!

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.300
I see. That's good to hear.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.090
Joe!

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.900
It's time to go.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.270
Let's move!

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.280
Okay, okay.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.950
Joe, where are you going?

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.080
Here. That's where.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.370
What are those?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.380
They're tickets to the Carlos-Harajima match.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.670
And it was Shiraki Yohko-san who invited me.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.420
Quit your blabbering!

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.480
Now let's go!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.670
I'll see you all later!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.220
Hey, wait up, old man!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.140
There he goes.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.640
Well, wasn't that disappointing?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.480
Maybe our bro isn't interested in anything besides boxing.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.520
Right, Noriko-chan?

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.190
What are you talking about, dummy?

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:36.640
Joe just has Carlos' match on his mind right now!

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.820
Carlos, huh?

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:40.900
You think so?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.230
Well, if you ask me, it's the Shiraki lady he's...

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.750
You know that's not true!

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.870
Stop it! Stop it!

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.510
Good afternoon! Apologies for the wait!

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.130
Oh, thank you kindly!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.300
If I may be blunt, what are your odds against Harajima?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.510
Odds? What does he mean?

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.310
L-Let's just say he'll do his best.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:16.770
I sure hope you get another lucky punch, 
like that one you delivered Nango the other day!

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.480
Whoever wins is a matter of luck.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.110
And Carlos here is certainly lucky.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.110
To be frank, I believe in Lady Luck.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.990
I see. That's very candid of you.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.070
Can we leave the questions at that?

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.080
All right! Just one photo!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.580
Okay, okay!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.380
Now, Carlos, strike a real strong pose!

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.340
Oh, wait! Pull your elbows in a bit more!

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:55.350
Good grief, why are foreigners so obsessed with poses?

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.310
That manager sure seemed apprehensive.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.820
Yeah, now I'm sure Harajima will crack the world rankings.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.580
Well done, Carlos!

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.330
You looked just like a frightened little lamb!

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.540
And you were quite the actor yourself, Robert.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.330
Well, this is my business, after all.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.390
But you can't use any so-called lucky punches against Harajima.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.760
Don't worry.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:34.440
I've thought up another way to make Carlos' victory seem like a coincidence.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.850
Hey, Carlos!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.620
Carlos, your lucky number is four.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.310
Take him down, Harajima!

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.140
Harajima!

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.140
And the match is finally on, folks!

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.980
The second fighter to challenge Carlos, ranked six in the world,

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.900
is the Japanese first-ranked bantamweight, Harajima Ryu!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.490
Nango suffered a regrettable defeat the other day,

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:34.360
but Harajima expressed confidence that he would take revenge before the match!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:37.580
And he's got a one-two punch in!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:38.660
Yeah, Harajima! Right there!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.290
Yeah! Right there, right there!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.200
One-two! One-two! One-two!

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.090
Joe...

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.680
Oh, no! Don't stop!

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.390
Use your feet! Your feet, Carlos!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.650
Yeah! Get him!

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.860
What could they be planning?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.910
<i>Carlos, your lucky number is four.</i>

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.660
Four... His lucky number is four...

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.000
A lucky punch is one thing.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.880
Two of them in the row won't make them so lucky.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.560
Harajima! Don't get cocky, idiot!

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.640
Keep your distance!

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.390
Oh, you're right!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:25.400
I almost forgot about the lucky punch...

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.890
or maybe I'm just pretending to let up on you!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.990
Take him down, Harajima!

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.990
Show him how high the level of Japanese boxing is!

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:49.340
Good grief. I know this was said during the Nango match,

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.840
but Carlos' attacks are just so awful!

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.550
Carlos is taking a heavy beating,

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:56.140
and his second, Robert, has a grave expression on his face!

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:33.300
How is Carlos going to cook Harajima's goose,

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.880
without revealing his true power?

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.270
Yeah, there! Right there, Harajima!

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.480
Rush him! Rush him!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.810
Kick his ass!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.070
Finish him off already!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.620
Get your guard up!

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:03.860
Circle him! Circle him!

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:13.710
Carlos is utterly trapped!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.210
Carlos can't do anything!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.310
Carlos is in danger!

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.560
With the third round finally over, Carlos Rivera is reeling!

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.070
He's thrown very few punches, and his knees are about to buckle!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.740
The reason he's still standing is because of Harajima's caution,

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.450
and his incredibly tough composition!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.660
You said it.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.540
I can barely believe he's ranked sixth in the world.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.580
Carlos...

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.020
His lucky number is four...

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.350
And now it's time for round four!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.280
Round four... Four... Lucky number...

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.820
I've got it!

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:21.860
This is the round...

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.240
Now go for it!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.670
Harajima wastes no time in delivering a one-two!

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:37.790
That was a full-on hit! Looks like this is it.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:49.600
Weave, Carlos! Weave, weave, weave!

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:50.930
Carlos!

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:05.070
Well, Coach, looks like I'm not gonna get a turn with him.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.400
Now that we know what a piece of trash he is,

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.580
we should've skipped Harajima and had him fight you right away.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.830
Then I could've made it straight into the world rankings...

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.170
What a crying shame.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.180
Go on! Finish him!

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.640
Get him, Harajima! Take him down!

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.850
Oh, Carlos, Carlos!

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.440
It's all over...

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.350
What's your problem, Rivera?

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.800
You go, Harajima!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.900
What the hell is Carlos thinking?

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.210
All right. Now!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.070
Go!

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:31.070
You did great! That round was yours!

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.630
Now remember, Harajima. You better watch out.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.470
If you aren't cautious, you'll end up just like Nango!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.590
Come on now, open up and drink.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.100
H-Harajima?

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.110
Hey, Harajima! What's happened to you?

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:03.060
Hey! Harajima!

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:04.940
Harajima!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.080
All right, seconds out!

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:16.450
Hey! I said seconds out!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.040
Can you hear me?

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.460
What in God's name happened?

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.590
What's the matter? Did something happen to Harajima?

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.510
Well... you see...

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.760
Hang on a moment, Carlos.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.720
Hey, what the hell are you doing, dumbass?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.680
Didn't you hear the bell?

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.440
<i>Hey, get a move on!</i>

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:40.680
<i>What is this?!</i>

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.280
Goddamn it!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.570
What's wrong?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:56.240
Oh, I think Harajima's just injured his leg.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:59.580
He's got a cramp in his calf.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.170
A cramp in his calf?

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:04.460
Yeah. A leg cramp, if you will.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.250
He's fought a hard fight.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.800
A leg cramp...

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.130
Well, that can be a problem...

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.890
So you don't reckon he'll be able to keep fighting?

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:17.350
No telling. He's in so much pain he can't even speak.

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.260
And he had his opponent on the ropes and all...

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:24.480
Well, if he can't leave his corner after the bell rings,

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:27.730
that's technically a TKO by forfeit...

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.230
I guess we have no choice.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.740
G-Guess we don't. It's a shame, but what can we do about it?

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.240
We have to follow the rules.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.250
Carlos Rivera!

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.890
Carlos!

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.560
Robert!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.690
Well played.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.150
That was an incredible act.

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:14.030
Carlos! You're a very, very lucky boy!

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:14.990
Lucky!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.950
Hey, what the hell just happened?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.710
This match is fixed!

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.760
<i>Allow me to explain the situation.</i>

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:35.010
<i>Harajima just had a severe cramp in his leg, and has thrown the match.</i>

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:39.560
<i>Therefore, according to the rules, Carlos Rivera wins by TKO!</i>

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.720
You dumbass!

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:45.720
You expect us to swallow that crock of shit?

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:48.730
That match was barely even boxing!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:48.730
<i>How could Rivera win by TKO?</i>

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:50.150
I want my money back!

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:57.190
Well, folks, that was the worst possible way to end the worst possible match!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.290
<i>Please, stop throwing things!</i>

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:01.330
<i>Please, stop throwing things!</i>

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.670
Well, coach, that was a real shame.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:06.750
You were this close...

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.210
I'll bet it was a big disappointment.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.250
So what are your present thoughts?

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.840
Leave us alone!

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:12.880
Just a quick word...

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:16.840
Come on, please have some pity and let him have his privacy!

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.930
Throw some water on him!

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:32.440
If anybody knew that Harajima Ryu actually lost consciousness,

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.650
that would be fatal to him!

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.530
I said pour some water, morons!

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.740
Right away, sir!

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:47.880
I was crushed the moment I noticed he'd passed out on his chair...

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.260
The reporters' eyes were on us by the ringside,

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:56.970
and the stands were full of disappointed fans.

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:59.140
So I came up with the cramp as an excuse,

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:03.220
and managed to avoid tarnishing his reputation as the first-ranked bantamweight...

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.200
What the hell happened to you?

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.500
Decided to take an afternoon nap in the ring?

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:29.880
I asked what the hell happened to you!?

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:32.960
Round...

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.960
Round four ended with Rivera's straight...

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.970
You mean that punch he threw right at the end?

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:48.070
I-I can't remember anything after he threw that punch...

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.570
Y-You mean that by the time you walked back to your chair like nothing had happened,

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:59.700
you had already been knocked unconscious?

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.450
Then, when your coach noticed,

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:07.080
he tried to cover up your unconsciousness to protect your reputation,

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:09.210
and came up with another excuse.

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:11.700
Carlos Rivera had that all planned out.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.550
Y-Yabuki!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.630
Carlos Rivera is a fearsome man indeed.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:21.840
How long has he been here?

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:26.680
I kept quiet about it since you all were busy.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:27.470
Son of a...

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.680
Hold on. No need to worry.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:33.680
I'm not gonna tell anyone about Harajima's secret KO.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.230
Not only would it make things worse for you,

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.700
but Rivera needs to make this victory seem like luck.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:46.370
So they can't let the secret out until they've scheduled a match with Tiger Ozaki.

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:50.840
Carlos Rivera...

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:54.630
He's one hell of a guy.

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:19.370
Our next target is Tiger Ozaki.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:24.200
So we just have to keep this farce up, right?

00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:29.320
Well then, what trick shall we use next?

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:54.650
Carlos Rivera...

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:16.340
For the first time in a long while...

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:19.710
you've made my blood boil.

00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:37.030
With his match with the Champion Tiger Ozaki before him,

00:24:37.410 --> 00:24:40.160
Carlos declares he will deliver a KO within one minute!

00:24:41.250 --> 00:24:43.580
Carlos finally shows his terrifying true colors!

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:46.260
And Carlos' eyes gleam as he bares his fangs!

00:24:47.010 --> 00:24:49.170
He attacks faster than the eye can follow!

00:24:49.170 --> 00:24:53.310
Carlos delivers the KO that he predicted as a challenge to Joe!

00:24:54.140 --> 00:25:01.270
Joe's wild instincts rise up to face Carlos' graceful yet dreadful challenge!

00:25:01.940 --> 00:25:05.230
Now, as Joe's match against his rival Carlos is set,

00:25:05.230 --> 00:25:07.650
and he burns with desire to defeat him,

00:25:07.650 --> 00:25:09.110
which way is tomorrow!?
